```{r observation data}
# Read in daily observation data
obs_data00 <- 
  read_csv(file = "../data/mastath-obs-day.csv", col_types = "fDnnnnnnnn") %>%
  filter(station_id != "USGS_Conte:O'Bear Brook sec 1 (Onset) [2722]", 
         station_id != "USGS_Conte:O'Bear Brook sec 15 (Onset) [2730]", 
         station_id != "USGS_Conte:O'Bear Brook Sec 1 (Solinst) [3886]") %>%
  droplevels()

# read in station site data
obs_station_data00 <- 
  read_csv(file = "../data/mastath-obs-stn.csv", col_types = "fifnnnn") %>%
  select(-station_name) %>%
  filter(station_id != "USGS_Conte:O'Bear Brook sec 1 (Onset) [2722]", 
         station_id != "USGS_Conte:O'Bear Brook sec 15 (Onset) [2730]", 
         station_id != "USGS_Conte:O'Bear Brook Sec 1 (Solinst) [3886]") %>%
  droplevels() %>%
  mutate(stn_id_num = as.numeric(station_id))
```


Some steps taken to ensure data quality were to filter out rows that had odd numbers of values used to calculated the daily temperature statistics. These odd values were either large or small. Large values greater than 288 (288 daily measurements indicates sensor readings every 5 minutes) were eliminated because they did not match up with associated regular measurements at high reading frequencies (e.g., 3 min interval = 480; 2 min interval = 720). Small values ranged from 2-11. Entries into the EcoSHEDS database likely had n_values = 1 when daily statistics were entered rather than the sensor reading time series data. This is why n_values = 1 were retained. Rows with n_values of 2 through 11 were removed because they can't be verified as individual sites or they have a sensor reading frequency that's unlikely to fully characterize the daily minimum, mean, or maximum statistics we are using.  


```{r station data join and data filtering}
obs_day_df <- obs_data00 %>% 
  mutate(station_id = as.factor(station_id)) %>%
  left_join(x=., 
            y= select(obs_station_data00, station_id, stn_id_num, comid), 
            by = "station_id") %>%
  filter(n_values < 289) %>%  # remove 33 rows with n_values greater than 288
  filter(n_values < 2 | n_values > 11)  # remove rows with values btwn 1 and 12
```


We set a 95% temperature data completeness requirement in order to include an observation site in the dependent variable data set. This 95% completeness requirements means 95% of the regularly-spaced sensor measurements within a day were available to calculate the daily statistics and 95% of the days within a month were available to calculate a monthly statistic. Since the data are daily statistics, we can only use the number of measurements used to calculated the daily statistics to verify if enough within-day readings were present to meet the 95% completeness requirements. For monthly statistics, we can use the daily statistics to ensure that 95% of the days in a month are present to calculated monthly statistics. We interpolated the missing daily values so that statistics weren’t potentially skewed by a missing day within a month. 



```{r July temp data 95% completeness check and interpolations}
obs_july_int_df <-  obs_day_df %>%
  mutate(smpl_date = date) %>% select(-date) %>%
  mutate(smpl_year = lubridate::year(smpl_date),
         smpl_month = lubridate::month(smpl_date),
         smpl_day = lubridate::day(smpl_date) ) %>%
  complete(., nesting(station_id, stn_id_num, smpl_year, smpl_month),
           smpl_day, fill = list(mean_temp_C = NA)) %>%
  mutate(smpl_date = make_date(smpl_year, smpl_month, smpl_day)) %>%
  relocate(smpl_date, .before = smpl_year) %>%
  group_by(station_id, smpl_year, smpl_month) %>%
  mutate(month_n = sum(!is.na(mean_temp_c))) %>% # counts total non-NA values
  relocate(month_n, .after = smpl_day) %>%
  filter(smpl_month == 7 & month_n == 31) %>%
  mutate(int_min_WT =  na.approx(min_temp_c, na.rm = FALSE),
         int_mean_WT = na.approx(mean_temp_c, na.rm = FALSE),
         int_max_WT =  na.approx(max_temp_c, na.rm = FALSE),
         int_min_AT =  na.approx(min_airtemp_c, na.rm = FALSE),
         int_mean_AT = na.approx(mean_airtemp_c, na.rm = FALSE),
         int_max_AT =  na.approx(max_airtemp_c, na.rm = FALSE),
         int_precipmm = na.approx(prcp_mm, na.rm = FALSE) ) %>%
  select(-ends_with("_c"), -prcp_mm) %>%
  arrange(smpl_date) %>% ungroup()
```


```{r calculate mean july stats for site-year combos}
obs_july_avg_df <- obs_july_int_df %>%
  group_by(station_id, stn_id_num, smpl_year) %>%
  summarize(avg_min_WT = mean(int_min_WT),
            avg_mean_WT = mean(int_mean_WT),
            avg_max_WT = mean(int_max_WT),
            avg_min_AT = mean(int_min_AT),
            avg_mean_AT = mean(int_mean_AT),
            avg_max_AT = mean(int_max_AT),
            sum_precipmm = sum(int_precipmm) ) %>%
  select(-starts_with("int_")) %>% ungroup() %>%
  mutate(ssnid = 10000 + row_number() ,
         stn_id_num = as.factor(stn_id_num)) %>%
  relocate(ssnid, .before = station_id) %>%
  droplevels()
```



```{r write out obs temp data for SSN modeling script}
write_csv(left_join(obs_july_avg_df, 
                    select(obs_station_data00, station_id, comid),
                    by = "station_id"), 
          file = "../data/obs_july_avg_df.csv")
```



